WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.136
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.137
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.372
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:07.473
I appreciate it.

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:08.507
Hey, this is exciting.

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:10.576
This Sunday is Mother's Day,
everyone.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:13.279
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.981
We love all the moms out there.

00:00:15.981 --> 00:00:18.150
The kids and I planned
something special for my wife.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.153
We made our own cards.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.186
There's gonna be
breakfast in bed.

00:00:21.186 --> 00:00:23.556
I booked her a mani-pedi,

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.059
whereas on Father's Day,
I got a Post-it note.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.763
It said, "We love Mom" on it.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:35.435
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:36.769
I read that over the years,

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:40.239
the average mom receives
45 pieces of homemade artwork.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:41.374
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.842
That's a lot.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.478
I'm sure after the first five,
even da Vinci's mom was like,

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.012
"How long before
I can chuck this thing?

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:49.815
I mean...is he watching?"

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.216
Yeah, Mother's Day
is almost here,

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:53.419
and if you're looking for
some last-minute inspiration,

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:54.954
you may like this commercial
I just saw.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.288
Check this out.

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:59.458
-Here at Zales, we know
how special moms are,

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:02.362
and that's why we have
the perfect gifts,

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.331
like a giant locket
that goes with nothing

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.667
even though she mentioned
wanting a manicure,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.436
or a diamond-encrusted
Mickey Mouse necklace,

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:12.338
even though she handed you
the number to a spa

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.340
with a note that said, "Buy
this."

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.411
Or a Casio watch that looks like
you got it from a claw machine,

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.113
even though
she literally screamed

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.615
"Running shoes" at you
over breakfast.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.750
Zales --

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.851
just get her
what she [bleep] wants.

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:28.321
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Aw, that's sweet, isn't it?

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:31.424
Kind of beautiful.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.758
Well, let's get to some news.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:35.562
Yesterday, President Biden
visited Louisiana.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.363
Did you see this?
-Yeah.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.166
And he opened his speech
with a story

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:43.002
about another time
that he visited the state.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.470
Listen to this.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:48.307
-First time I came down here,
was a guy named Russell Long,

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:49.942
who I served with.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:53.045
I was 29 years old
when I got elected,

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:56.582
and I went to see Russell Long.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:59.552
He said, "How much money
did you spend in your campaign?"

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:03.155
"About," I said,
"Little over $285,000."

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:07.326
But then I had to borrow
some money to get through it.

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:09.495
And he said,
"Good thing you won."

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:11.064
And I said, "How's that?"

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:14.333
He said, "Well," he said, "You
got yourself

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.669
a $38,000 'dee-ficit.'"

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.836
And I said, "Yes, sir."

00:02:17.836 --> 00:02:19.839
He said, "Well, if you had won,

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.507
you just have
a plain old dee-ficit.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.275
Now you can have
a dee-ficit party."

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:25.711
[ Laughs ]

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.647
God, he was amazing.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.816
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.854
-You know you're talking
for a while

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.356
when you watch the tide come in
and go back out, right?

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:38.657
You know that.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:39.759
I'll tell you one thing.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.093
Biden sure doesn't have
a "dee-ficit"

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.863
of long, rambling stories.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:44.964
Can we check in
on Biden right now?

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.298
Where is he? What's he doing?

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:47.433
[ Crickets chirping ]
-It's hard to believe that...

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.767
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
You already said --

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.036
Yeah. I believe it.
I believe it.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.371
-Hideout.
-Gosh. Holy moly.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.072
-Hogging the entire time.

00:02:54.072 --> 00:02:56.642
-Well, things just keep
getting worse for Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.411
[ Audience member whoops ]
I saw that 'cause of his gr--

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.312
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:01.914
I saw that 'cause of his
growing legal bills,

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:04.984
Rudy had to lay off several
members of his entourage.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.118
-Mm.

00:03:06.118 --> 00:03:07.853
-It's the worst news
those people have gotten

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:08.988
since they found out

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.356
that they were in
Rudy Giuliani's entourage.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.825
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:13.926
-Me?

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:15.228
I'm in his entourage?

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.396
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:18.898
I didn't know
he had an entourage.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.833
I always assumed those people
with him were orderlies.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.202
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.470
Well, this made me laugh.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.072
Last night on "Jeopardy!,"
I saw a contestant

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.906
ran into a little trouble
answering a question.

00:03:27.906 --> 00:03:29.175
Check this out.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.244
Hot Stuff for $1,000.
-Hot Stuff.

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:39.618
-Steve.

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:41.120
-Is it calzone?

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.989
[ Laughter ]
-No.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.724
[ Beep beep beep ]
"What are ovens?"

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.526
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.427
-Calzone?

00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:49.595
-He's like, "Of course,
I'm sorry.

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:51.197
Who -- Who is calzone?"

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:54.133
When he said that, other
contestants were thinking,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.201
"You idiot,"

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.202
while everyone
at home was shouting,

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.738
"What are Hot Pockets?"

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:01.474
They actually are 800 degrees.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.408
Well, here's some news here.

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:03.576
This isn't good for those of you

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.512
trying to take
an Uber or Lyft this summer.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.913
Listen to this.

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:09.915
-We're back with a heads-up
for Lyft and Uber customers.

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:11.584
A shortage of drivers

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.652
is making the cost of
the rideshares

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:15.755
much higher
than they used to be.

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:18.657
-No way. I have to pay more
for Uber now?

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:20.559
-Yeah, sorry about that, Tariq.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:21.894
-It's all good.

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.996
I actually bought a Hyundai
last week,

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:25.631
so I'll drive myself.

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:26.733
It's fine.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.868
-Oh.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.702
-"Oh," what?

00:04:30.702 --> 00:04:31.971
-Roll the clip.

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:36.308
-Hyundai is recalling
more than 390,000 vehicles

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:38.978
for two problems
that can cause fires.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:40.780
-What?!

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.016
Now how am I supposed to
get around this summer?

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:45.284
I guess I'll just sit at home

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.886
and eat some ice cream
or sherbet.

00:04:47.886 --> 00:04:49.288
-Well...

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:51.024
-Don't you dare.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.258
-Roll the clip.

00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:56.696
-Almost 100 popular ice cream
brands and sherbets

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:59.331
have been recalled
over possible listeria.

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:00.933
-Well, at least I can eat

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:04.036
some of that chocolate shell
topping that goes on ice cream.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:07.707
Here's hoping there's no recall
they want to make me aware of.

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.442
-A recall we want to
make you aware of.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:11.477
Hershey's is voluntarily
recalling

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.345
some of its chocolate
shell topping.

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:15.581
-Come on!
-I'm sorry.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.350
Tariq, there's got to be
something else you enjoy.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.251
What's your favorite snack?

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:22.788
-Oh, that's easy. The Ruffles
All Dressed potato chips.

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.957
-Frito Lay is issuing
a voluntary recall

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:29.094
of select bags of Ruffles
All Dressed potato chips.

00:05:29.094 --> 00:05:30.562
-What do I even have left,

00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:32.331
the beans in my cabinets?

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:33.799
-Check your cabinets.

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:37.804
There's a recall of black beans
and chili beans nationwide.

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:38.938
-I give up.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:41.073
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:44.309
[ Applause ]

00:05:44.309 --> 00:05:46.612
This summer is a bust!

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:49.281
-Oh, come on, Tariq!
Look at the bright side.

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:51.684
I mean, aren't you going on a
double date this weekend?

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.653
-That's true.
I'm looking forward to that.

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:55.120
-Yeah. Who are you going with,
again?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.255
-Bill and Melinda Gates.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.090
[ Laughter ]
-Let's just move on.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.325
Let's just move on.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:00.693
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.195
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:06.199
-"The beans in my cabinets?"

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:09.635
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.836
Oh.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:10.836 --> 00:06:12.772
-Oh, man.
-[ Laughing ] And finally --

00:06:14.172 --> 00:06:16.875
It's such a good read.

00:06:16.875 --> 00:06:19.011
Finally, I heard that Rome
just unveiled

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.045
a new vending machine

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:21.613
that makes hot pizza
in three minutes.

00:06:21.613 --> 00:06:23.182
-Ooh.
-Here it is.

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:24.383
Yeah, look at that.

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:27.119
And if you buy a vending-
machine pizza in Rome,

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:28.654
it also comes with
a T-shirt that says,

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:30.555
"Rob me.
I'm not from here.

00:06:30.555 --> 00:06:32.458
-Guys, as I mentioned,
Mother's Day is this weekend,

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:35.060
and a lot of people are running
out of time to find a gift.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.729
Well, luckily, we here
at "The Tonight Show"

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:37.863
think ahead,

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:39.398
which is why we're releasing
some special

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:41.066
"Tonight Show"
Mother's Day coupons...

00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:42.568
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:45.170
...to help you out.
Take a look at some of these.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:46.305
First, we've got...

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:51.310
-Oh.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.645
-You get a free --
-Yeah.

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:54.213
-That'll come in handy.

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:55.414
It's Chris Hemsworth,
by the way.

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:56.682
-Oh, every time.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:57.750
Next, there is...

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:04.523
"Oh, yeah, yeah.
That's funny, Mom. It's great."

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:06.025
After that, we have...

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:12.497
Any "Bridgerton" fans?

00:07:12.497 --> 00:07:14.467
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:15.501
-Next up...

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:20.573
-Oh.
-"Yeah, that's right.

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.408
I know. Tom is doing well, Mom."

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:24.310
[ Applause ]

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.411
Next, there's...

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:33.386
"I'm not even
in that state, Mom."

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:35.922
Next up, we have...

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:46.699
-Wow, I like that.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.767
-"Well, let's just
not even watch it."

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:50.235
-Hit "Input."

00:07:50.235 --> 00:07:52.104
-"Just hit 'Input," Mom."

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:54.406
-I don't know.
"Now it says 'HDMI-3.'"

00:07:54.406 --> 00:07:56.842
-No, just hit --
-"I don't know."

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.911
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:00.246
-And finally, we've got...

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:04.683
-Aww. We love you.

00:08:04.683 --> 00:08:06.853
Enjoy those
Mother's Day coupons.

